    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=8,\\ y=-2$.",
      "worked": "The chain gives $2x+3y=10$ and $x-y=10$. Isolate $x$ in the second equation, then substitute into the first.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=y+10\\\\2(y+10)+3y&=10\\\\5y&=-10\\\\y&=-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBack-substitute:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=-2+10\\\\x&=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original expressions:\n\n$$2(8)+3(-2)=10,\\qquad 8-(-2)=10.$$\n\nThus $x=8$ and $y=-2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
